{"availability":"available","full":"CVERInc/demodeck","name":"demodeck","description":"A polished dark control-panel template for open-source demos. Pure CSS + a tiny behavior layer, zero dependencies.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-28T12:46:18Z","updated":"2026-07-05T22:43:37Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["control-panel","css","dark-theme","dashboard","demo","open-source","playground","showcase","ui-kit"],"demo":"https://oss.cver.net/demodeck/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.295Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.295Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.295Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.295Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A dark \"control panel\" template for open-source demos. A header, a two-column layout, and a kit of dark-themed controls — segmented buttons, sliders, color fields, toggles, styled selects, popovers, a live console terminal, and a copyable code box. Drop a live preview on the right and you have an interactive playground for your library in minutes.","Every good OSS project deserves a demo where people can play with it — toggle options, drag sliders, watch the result update live. Building that chrome from scratch each time is a chore. demodeck gives you the whole interactive shell, dark out of the box, so you can spend your effort on the thing you're actually demoing.","It pairs naturally with a live preview — including liquidframe if your project is mobile/web UI."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CVERInc/demodeck/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"012dbecab3195a135eadffe17f973a058a74bc22a805aae23acf6e5c7316d873","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.471Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:00:39.471Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A dark \"control panel\" template for open-source demos. A header, a two-colum